  "difficulty_reason": "The authors derive a local flat-intersection multiplication rule (Lemma 2.6) and construct a weighted bijection between compatible flat insertions and one-vertex binary-tree extensions. Iterating that bijection in a single induction proves a uniform flat-filled increasing binary-tree expansion of an arbitrary product of hypersimplex classes in the integral matroid Chow ring, carrying the exact v-compatibility condition and both the over-intersection and multiplicity weights. This is above the level of applying the degree map or Hodge inequalities: the psi_F flag decomposition of section 2 and the whole compatibility-and-weight apparatus of section 5 must be built first and then combined without losing either weight function.",
